2. Definitions.- In this Ordinance, unless the context otherwise requires, the following expressions shall have the meanings hereby respectively assigned to them, that is to say__
(a) ‘child’ means a person who has not completed the age of sixteen years;
(aa) “Government” means the Government of West Pakistan;
(b) “guardian” includes any person who has accepted or assumed the care or custody of any child;
(c) “parent” means the father or mother of a child;
(d) ‘prescribed’ means prescribed by rules made under this Ordinance;
(dd) “Smallpox Eradication Officer” means an officer appointed by Government to perform the functions and duties of the Smallpox Eradication Officer under this Ordinance;
(e) ‘Superintendent of Vaccination’ means a person appointed to perform the duties of Superintendent of Vaccination under this Ordinance;
7(f) “unprotected child” and “unprotected person” mean respectively a child or a person who has not been protected from smallpox by having had that disease, or by having not been successfully vaccinated, and who has not been certified

1Substituted by the West Pakistan Ordinance No. XVI of 1969, s.2(2).
2Inserted by the West Pakistan Ordinance No. XVI of 1969, s. 3(i).
3Re-lettered by the Ordinance ibid.

under this Ordinance to be insusceptible to vaccination;
(g) ‘vaccination’ means the introduction of Vaccinia Virus (Lymph) into the skin in order to confer protection against smallpox; and
(h) ‘vaccinator’ means any person appointed to perform the operation of vaccination.

15. Power of Government to make rules.- (1) Government may frame rules for the purpose of carrying into effect the provisions of this Ordinance.

(2) In particular and without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers, Government may frame rules for all or any of the following purposes, namely:__
(a) prescribing qualifications, conditions of service and uniform for vaccinators;
(aa) prescribing the authorities by whom appointments under this Ordinance are to

1Substituted by the West Pakistan Ordinance No. XVI of 1969, s. 9.

be made;
(b) regulating the manner in which the Superintendent of Vaccination shall exercise his duties under this Ordinance;
(c) prescribing the lymph that may be used for vaccination;
(d) * * * * * * *
(e) prescribing registers to be maintained under this Ordinance; and
(f) prescribing the forms for notices and certificates.

16. Repeal.- The following enactments are hereby repealed:__
(a) the Vaccination Act, 1880 (XIII of 1880);
(b) the Sind Vaccination Act, 1892 (Sind I of 1892);

(c) the Bombay District Vaccination Act, 1892 (Bombay I of 1892), as applicable to the former State of Khairpur;
(d) the Punjab Vaccination Law Amendment Act, 1925 (Punjab IX 1925);
(e) the Punjab Vaccination Law Amendment Act, 1929 (Punjab II of 1929); and
(f) the North-West Frontier Province Vaccination Law (Amendment) Act, 1947 (N.W.F.P.
XI of 1947).

